{"packet_id":"D026-01","doc_id":"D026","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Application screening fee cap and refund rules","requirement":"A landlord or agent may charge an application screening fee no greater than actual out-of-pocket costs and no more than $30 per applicant, CPI-adjusted annually. The landlord must provide an itemized receipt and refund unused or unconsidered application fees.","key_value":"$30 per applicant, CPI-adjusted annually","coverage_conditions":"Residential rental property applicants; a landlord is an owner of residential rental property. Applies to entities or individuals requesting to rent, act as guarantor, or cosign.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Residential rentals; no building age or unit limits stated."},"exemptions":"Does not preempt federal or state housing assistance program rules on deposits and fees. A landlord need not refund a fee to an applicant denied after consideration for not meeting criteria.","penalty":null,"effective_date":"2026-01-01","citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.6","quoted_span":"In no case shall the amount of the application screening fee charged by the landlord or their agent be greater than thirty dollars ($30) per applicant. The thirty dollar ($30) application screening fee may be adjusted annually by the landlord or their agent commensurate with an increase in the Consumer Price Index, beginning on January 1, 1998.","interaction":"Does not preempt federal or state housing assistance program rules governing deposits and fees.","confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D026-01","doc_id":"D026","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Application order and first-qualified applicant screening rule","requirement":"A landlord must give screening criteria in writing with the application and consider completed applications in the order received. The first applicant who meets the criteria is approved for tenancy; fees may only be charged once an application is considered.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Residential rental property applicants; applies when a landlord or agent charges or collects an application screening fee.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Residential rentals; screening process when fee charged."},"exemptions":"Inadvertent concurrent-application fee collection is not a violation if refunded within seven days or applied to another unit at applicant's discretion; no refund owed to an applicant denied after consideration.","penalty":null,"effective_date":"2026-01-01","citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.6","quoted_span":"(i) Completed applications are considered, as provided for in the landlord’s established screening criteria, in the order in which the completed applications were received. The landlord’s screening criteria shall be provided to the applicant in writing together with the application form.\n(ii) The first applicant who meets the landlord’s established screening criteria is approved for tenancy.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
